  "notes": [
    "This amendment chains directly to the byte-exact immutable original consumed-test ledger. No prior Stage-90 amendment, result, prediction surface, scratch directory, or checkpoint is a parent or input.",
    "B, U, and all eight frozen A1 probability surfaces are recomputed under experiment-owned namespaces and globally sealed before any label capability opens. Each whole case or group c is held out from its same-H support labels; every endpoint plan and aggregate method decision is sealed before terminal c labels open.",
    "Directional support gain is computed from additive pooled confusion counts on the two B-defined hard-flip branches. The donor prior for candidate e uses equal-center query contributions q outside H and e. Each of the nine frozen K-by-w arms ranks legal sources by G, admits OFF at score zero, and retains its identity even when another arm selects the same endpoint.",
    "The matched G control runs the identical arm and probability-composition pipeline with S set equal to G. Nominal intervals, delete-one summaries, and the candidate-identity null are descriptive only and cannot authorize a route, action, policy, promotion, deployment, or later experiment.",
    "This terminal diagnostic is bounded by the prior finding of no stable incremental target-support advantage versus G and cannot convert consumed-test adaptation into fresh evidence."
